Subject: [PATCH] null renderer: one layer at its own size

A frame with one layer, the usual case, goes to the frontend at the
layer's size, without scaling it to 1280x720 first: the frontend scales it
to its screen anyway, and on a slow CPU (the PS4's) scaling twice costs a
few milliseconds a frame. With more layers, the source column of each
pixel is computed once per layer instead of once per pixel.
---
